'''Emanuel Zanders''' (born July 31, 1951) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] [[offensive lineman]] in the [[National Football League]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.clarionledger.com/story/sports/college/jackson-state/2024/03/14/emanuel-zanders-jackson-state-football-nfl-career-new-orleans-saints/72944843007/ | title=How Jackson State football teammate's tip to a scout launched Emanuel Zanders' 8-year NFL career | work=[[Clarion-Ledger]] | date=March 14, 2024 | accessdate=21 January 2025 | author=Keith, J. T.}}</ref> He played for the [[New Orleans Saints]] from 1974 to 1980, and he played for the [[Chicago Bears]] in 1981. He played [[college football]] at [[Jackson State University]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Emanuel Zanders |url=https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/Z/ZandEm20.htm |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221013051732/https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/Z/ZandEm20.htm |archive-date=2022-10-13 |access-date=2023-04-17 |website=Pro-Football-Reference.com |language=en}}</ref>

Zanders is a member of the New Orleans Saints Hall of Fame 25 Years All-Time Team.{{Citation needed|date=April 2023}} He was a Saints captain from 1976 to 1979.{{Citation needed|date=April 2023}} In 1979, he was voted as the Saints Offensive Lineman of the Year.{{Citation needed|date=April 2023}} Other honors Zanders received in his professional career was the Soulful Saints, Inc. Offensive Player of the Year, 1978 and the National Sports Foundation Offensive Player of the Year, 1980.{{Citation needed|date=April 2023}}

Zanders was inducted into the Jackson State University Sports Hall of Fame in 2004.{{Citation needed|date=April 2023}}

